// Pull request: #6659 new: Transparent Tribe (APT36) PcDirvs loader, public core HTA and Crimson RAT runner
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6659
// Pull request author: sohankanna
// Change: new rule
// Title: Transparent Tribe PcDirvs Loader File Creation
// Sigma ID: 7735e9b5-8afd-4727-a0f0-eb1ba2c6be80
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: @sohankanna
// Date: 2026-11-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, persistence, privilege-escalation, T1574.001, G0134
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects the creation of files used by the PcDirvs loader of Transparent Tribe (APT36), as
//   reported by CYFIRMA in December 2025. In this campaign against Indian government entities, a LNK
//   named "NCERT-Whatsapp-Advisory.pdf.lnk" installs a remote MSI. The MSI drops "pdf.dll" and a
//   malicious "wininet.dll" into "C:\ProgramData\PcDirvs\", then drops and runs "PcDirvs.exe". A
//   "PcDirvs.hta" script adds "PcDirvs.exe" to the Run key for persistence.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.cyfirma.com/research/apt36-lnk-based-malware-campaign-leveraging-msi-payload-delivery/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/0d96dbbaf239f29b10f0dea2f2a15c27dcbb3659/rules-emerging-threats/2025/TA/Transparent-Tribe/file_event_win_apt_transparent_tribe_pcdirvs_loader.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\ProgramData\\PcDirvs\\" and (FolderPath endswith "\\pdf.dll" or FolderPath endswith "\\wininet.dll")) or (FolderPath contains "\\ProgramData\\" and (FolderPath endswith "\\PcDirvs.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\PcDirvs.hta"))
